%N A183888 Number of arrangements of n+3 numbers in 0..5 with each number being the sum mod 6 of three others.
%H A183888 R. H. Hardin, <a href="/A183888/b183888.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..58</a>
%H A183888 <a href="/index/Rec#order_12">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (24,-252,1540,-6126,16764,-32444,44844,-44025,29996,-13488,3600,-432).
%F A183888 From _Mikhail Smirnov_, Nov 11 2026: (Start)
%F A183888 a(n) = 6^(n+3) - (2*n + 6)*3^(n+3) - (n^2 + 8*n + 16)*2^(n+5) - (5*n^5 + 99*n^4 + 509*n^3 + 693*n^2 - 1090*n - 2592)/6 for n >= 5.
%F A183888 G.f.: x * (8 + 790*x - 1400*x^2 - 47350*x^3 + 253964*x^4 - 190946*x^5 - 1510216*x^6 + 2426114*x^7 + 11418092*x^8 - 54686688*x^9 + 111323032*x^10 - 135460008*x^11 + 105254688*x^12 - 51517440*x^13 + 14549760*x^14 - 1814400*x^15) / ((1 - x)^6 * (1 - 2*x)^3 * (1 - 3*x)^2 * (1 - 6*x)). (End)
